# Foreign keys — the star center

## One FK per dimension

- `order_date_key`, `customer_key`, `product_key`, `channel_key`, `promotion_key`
- Each points at a dimension's **surrogate PK**
- Fact stores the **key**, never the descriptive text

## Every BI query is a star-join

```sql
SELECT p.product_line, SUM(f.line_total)
FROM   fact_sales f
JOIN   dim_product p ON f.product_key = p.product_key
GROUP BY p.product_line
```
- Measures from the **centre**, labels & filters from the **points**

## Why narrow integer keys

- **Fast joins** · **small storage**
- **Absorb dimension change** (SCD) without touching the fact
